# DocuTrust -- registry routing for org-owned scopes.
#
# A package published under an org-owned scope resolves ONLY from the org's
# registry of record. npm does not fall back: when that registry answers 404,
# the install stops rather than trying the public registry. Measured, not
# assumed -- Project 2 Phase 4.
#
# The registry of record is GitHub Packages, because the source lives on
# GitHub and that is where an org-owned package would be published.
#
# The one value this must never carry is registry.npmjs.org. Pinning our own
# scope to the public registry would not be a defence -- it would be the
# vulnerability, because a public package taking an internal name is exactly
# the attack this line exists to stop.
#
# Nothing in the tree is published under this scope today, so the pin is inert
# until someone introduces one -- and it is then the thing that stops a public
# package taking the name. Add one line per scope the org publishes under.
@docutrust:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com/
